Band Visual & Press Photoshoot Prompt: A stark, high-contrast black and white photograph in a derelict, echoing fishing hut overlooking a grey, churning sea. The three women of The Glacial Hearth Witches stand clustered, half-shrouded in oversized, roughly textured hand-knitted black shawls, their faces obscured by deep shadows, revealing only slivers of their intense, sorrowful expressions. Aksel's gnarled hands are frozen mid-knit, the impossibly long needles gleaming menacingly, connected by thick cables to a jury-rigged vintage tube amplifier crackling on a rough wooden crate. The Fjordsdottir sisters stand behind her, one with her hands poised over the imposing, dark polished 'Hval-Organ,' its pipes resembling ancient skeletal ribs, the other gripping a heavily scarred upright bass with a single flickering bare bulb casting a harsh halo around its distressed headstock. The air feels heavy, cold, pregnant with unspoken grief and raw, ancestral power.

Descriptive Mood or Vibe: Profound, elegiac sorrow tinged with raw, defiant energy and spectral nostalgia. It’s like discovering a forgotten, heartbreaking folk tune played through a rusty car stereo at the edge of the world.

